 "_about": "SINGLE-TRANSLATION SHELF: one-off translations of medieval and early texts, each by a translator with no other book to shelve: the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle (Ingram), Saxo Grammaticus (Elton), the Táin (Faraday; Dunn), the Chanson de Roland (Rabillon), Tristan and Iseult (Belloc), the High History of the Holy Graal (Evans), Barlaam and Ioasaph (Woodward and Mattingly), sagas, Old English poems, the Ship of Fools (Barclay, 1509), Camões's Lusiad (Mickle), Villani, the Hypnerotomachia (1592) and others. Each title gates on its own translator (_surname_by_slug). US public domain. Added 2026-10-10 by lane C (round 40); Adam may veto. No uids minted.",
